		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " A paren pair around an instantiation expression stays when a second type argument",
			"start": 20,
			"end": 104
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " list follows its close, whatever that list belongs to: a `new`, a call, a tagged",
			"start": 106,
			"end": 189
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " template, or another instantiation. Bare, the `<` opening the second list is a token",
			"start": 191,
			"end": 278
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " tsc's grammar never takes a first list ahead of, so `f<T><U>(x)` is the comparison",
			"start": 280,
			"end": 365
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " `f < T > <U>(x)`, with a type assertion on its right.",
